  "assumptionsNotes": [
    "First-year revenue, gross margin and operating profit are consensus inputs, not independently predicted outcomes. Net interest $0.1B, 15% tax extended beyond Q1, 155M constant diluted shares and $0.28B SBC growing 6% are assumptions; Q1 tax/shares and SBC range have company guidance support.",
    "Reported end-market sales are not reportable profit segments. FY2027 mix extends Q4 FY2026 mix. End-market shipment indices include bit/content and mix changes; they are not independently disclosed physical volumes. Product margins are undisclosed; costs are allocated by reference revenue and 80% of own-company D&A is manufacturing.",
    "FY2028\u201330 reference cost and opex budgets allocate management average 80% GM and 75% OM evenly. FY2028 revenue uses consensus $58.44B, followed by distinct shipment growth. Targets are conditional, not a promise of yearly margins. FY2028 modeled EPS is allowed to differ from consensus.",
    "In target years 25% of cash manufacturing cost is fixed and 75% follows each market shipment index relative to the frozen reference path. Thereafter variable unit cost falls 7.5% and fixed cost rises 3% annually. Cash opex rises 6% after FY2030. No undisclosed NBM floor or HBF commercial revenue is assumed.",
    "FCFF = after-tax operating income after economic SBC + own-company D&A - direct cash capex - net JV funding - working-capital increase - unallocated cash allowance. JV depreciation embedded in purchased wafer cost is never added back as Sandisk D&A. Net funding is additional to wafer purchases, not gross JV capex.",
    "Direct capex, JV funding and own D&A schedules are assumptions. The combined >$31B announcement is neither entirely Sandisk cash nor a disclosed net funding schedule. JV funding budgets include incremental equipment/leases, building prepayment timing and supply fee cash timing net of expense; exact allocation and credits are unknown.",
    "The cash allowance is the difference between a reference cash bridge and 50% adjusted-FCF margin during FY2028\u201330, before the separate after-tax SBC charge. Its composition is unknown. It is frozen independently of edits and scales with physical volume, not ASP. Later per-volume continuation is assumed. The comparison includes a 0\u2013200% allowance sensitivity.",
    "Reference working capital uses 50 receivable days, 130 inventory days, 65 trade-payable days and 1% sales operating accruals. Opening NWC excludes contract/refund liabilities, taxes, leases and uncertain accrued expenses. Capital payables are assumed settled in cash capex. Customer advances/deposits are excluded from new FCFF and fully reserved once from existing cash.",
    "July cash, marketable securities with a 20% haircut, zero reported borrowing, current/noncurrent taxes plus tax indemnity, full deferred tax, and $1B operating reserve build equity value. Flash Ventures equity/prepayment assets are operating assets and are not added again. Normal operating lease costs remain in cash expenses; lease guarantees are not all treated as funded debt. Tax receivables and other investments are omitted.",
    "No future repurchase is assumed merely because $15.5B is authorized. Guided diluted shares are a valuation proxy and kept fixed; future SBC is expensed with no addback. Reported July outstanding shares differ from this diluted denominator.",
    "Estimated interim cash uses uniform FY2027 cash generation to October 9; it is unverified. The full year incorporates stronger quarters than Q1 guidance, so this may overstate elapsed cash. The comparison separately removes that credit for all companies.",
    "After 2027\u201334 explicit years, growth, economic operating margin and net investment fade for four years, then a 2039 terminal period uses 2% growth, 25% after-tax incremental ROIC and 50% operating margin. These are valuation assumptions. Unknown explicit cash allowances are folded into total reinvestment during the fade rather than claimed as separately verified perpetual costs. A persistent extra 5% revenue cash drain is tested separately.",
    "Nominal USD discount is 12%; annual cash is discounted to the quote date using fiscal year-end approximations. Funding checks reserve claims conservatively, include haircutted marketable equities as realizable funds, and do not verify intra-year liquidity."
  ],
